{"title":"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be different points on a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is not a diameter. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangent line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8fe0bc1f0ab90d60df20bc9e4ccac77d35238e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen on the shorter arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> so that the circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fad291ff3531d1021dee6e5ee069902abcf6a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JST$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> at two distinct points. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the common point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> that is closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59b9a6c6724df7384848b8ea1772a120b9e2652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017_IMO_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4f/2017_IMO_4.png/500px-2017_IMO_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"190\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4f/2017_IMO_4.png/750px-2017_IMO_4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4f/2017_IMO_4.png/1000px-2017_IMO_4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We construct inversion which maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> into the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> into  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd137cd66e833f22447e7410bc31659ff08676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> Than we prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd137cd66e833f22447e7410bc31659ff08676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e84c03655ef5dc1a5d506d6462efe420bb7cde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RJSK$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4527239652fc758c4691f2796f0342ecf04f10fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle RSJ = \\angle RKJ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad4497e8e5db8e0f56cd22a5346e2e8261cfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46476845f6e911724ec614c4a0ecbd4f03e32de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle RSJ = \\angle TAJ \\implies AT||RK.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We construct circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> which maps  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> into  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd137cd66e833f22447e7410bc31659ff08676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e95760f6e3b1430c91ddf4f0a381db05cfe701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\omega \\cap RT \\implies RC^2 = RS \\cdot RT.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"279\" height=\"17\" /> Inversion with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> swap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c438cde8822d162cccc5c2872c4f299bdd1898ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\implies  \\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> maps into  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f81c350201c2544c12ccd486493fbb123e3b2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma (\\Gamma = \\Gamma&#39;).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd137cd66e833f22447e7410bc31659ff08676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Inversion with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />  maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb790556c91143b323450e791cf380a032b4edbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> belong <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f9066c5338f2e2f440139256583e3e8f54e2934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> circle  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/adda40b46cdc7f855f70e3dd7db82f470e8a5a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;SR = \\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" /> is the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/2181b109c12b979b3f5c904bb5b8f49c00298eff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039546635948735c501b8cf32a7a72f03c56fa84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> is the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at this inversion, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db58e16f444867bf106c566b8abe9f018811585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = AR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1603310a6bfb8542204de0e46b0e4484d3897a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5b226f3129c8216aa565d9c0eb2826ebb1df91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;T||AR.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb790556c91143b323450e791cf380a032b4edbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is image K at this inversion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f971bb54ccc8899cedaa620aeb0c884b7c9cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies K \\in RK&#39; \\implies RK&#39;||AT \\implies ARK&#39;T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"20\" /> is parallelogram.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e601385e44ff8092882775a29fbce9cae5db9596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RT \\implies S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of symmetry of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41a2548581d3ab836274856f6efa53e2d6f0c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ATK&#39;R \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0baf7a36431503dbf9696ea7f1cb1a781027fda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle RSK&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> is symmetrical to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427a2fccba5bf615346f305beff7fcc11c34da59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle TSA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fd0499582e4b10451ca62759d3f56daee0cbf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />  is symmetrical to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fd0499582e4b10451ca62759d3f56daee0cbf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is symmetrycal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7e49ad93a99ed6dcafd1c6acba511a181ab6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> and on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d73aa52ccb6cac80c822299746783e62f8c0ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1 \\implies \\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4184c9d3dafd6b83688d6a0792e8769b9e4b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1 \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd137cd66e833f22447e7410bc31659ff08676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017_IMO_4a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4b/2017_IMO_4a.png/500px-2017_IMO_4a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"254\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4b/2017_IMO_4a.png/750px-2017_IMO_4a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4b/2017_IMO_4a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We use the tangent-chord theorem: the angle formed between a chord and a tangent line to a circle is equal to the inscribed angle on the other side of the chord.\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e84c03655ef5dc1a5d506d6462efe420bb7cde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RJSK$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4527239652fc758c4691f2796f0342ecf04f10fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle RSJ = \\angle RKJ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Quadrangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad4497e8e5db8e0f56cd22a5346e2e8261cfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91ce123a4f78bb75a20f8ec83b90bc1724b8af8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle RSJ = \\angle TAJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/069e26f335bc2ae5663487de879b0b6907df73ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies AT||RK.\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(One can use Reim’s theorem – it is shorter way.)\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fd0499582e4b10451ca62759d3f56daee0cbf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156c646394900ec99b5cd49941ab05769ad0b204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ATBR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is parallelogram.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc1d66dcb17fefc616119a2f7cae33e6d5d8038.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle KST = \\angle SRK + \\angle SKR = \\angle KRA\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e433e66ef18d3d6cd03e722204ee3dae31d693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle RBT = \\angle RAT \\implies \\angle KST + \\angle KBT = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"377\" height=\"16\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018b92b0e261457493f454bb60a9917fe7352c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies SKBT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9b5c2b0d9ba1c5f6417a9993359f725779649f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle SBK = \\angle STK  = \\angle SAT \\implies\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Inscribed angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fb1f5bec96d559c23e55bebf46e34342934e28e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma (\\angle SAT)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> is equal to angle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> and chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/7150143170fdc1d1a1b21200579b330bf9d5fae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ST \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f71aa02ce528c94f319c81953decacafa6df0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> by the inverse of tangent-chord theorem.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO\" title=\"2017 IMO\">2017 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003832\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 535/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHig